- op: create  # 72be
  at: '2026-07-29T08:46:52Z'  # 72be
  by: agent  # 72be
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 72be
  clock: 1  # 72be
  nonce: 72be  # 72be
  data:  # 72be
    kind: work_item  # 72be
    title: "tracker auto-sync amended a feature-branch commit and destroyed its message; auto-pr's git-note net captured the post-loss body"  # 72be
    status: todo_hard  # 72be
    priority: 1  # 72be
    parent:  # 72be
    tags:  # 72be
    - infra  # 72be
    isbefore: []  # 72be
    duplicate_of: []  # 72be
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 72be
    pr_ref:  # 72be
    description: "The tracker auto-sync ran `git commit --amend` on a FEATURE-BRANCH commit it did\nnot author, replacing that commit's message with its own. The code survived; the\ncommit message was destroyed, and the git-notes safety net captured the wrong\nthing because it ran afterwards.\n\nLive instance 2026-07-29, PR #67 (WI-zugob producer batch 1):\n\n  reflog (bottom-up)\n    HEAD@{3}  checkout: dev -> jgstern-agent/fix/route-kind-slot-sweep-batch1\n    HEAD@{2}  commit (amend): tracker: 6 files (104 ops) - WI-tugab, WI-zugob...\n    HEAD@{1}  checkout: route-kind-slot-sweep-batch1 -> dev\n\n  result on dev\n    4062aa43b8  tracker: 6 files (104 ops)   <- 6 .ops files (correct, the sync's own)\n    cf955a0be1  tracker: 6 files (104 ops)   <- MY 7 CODE FILES, wearing the sync's message\n\n`cf955a0be1` contains .ci/affected-tests.txt, CHANGELOG.md, the route-parity\ngate and the four migrated analyzers -- and its subject claims it is a tracker\nop sync. `git log` for this change is now actively misleading: searching the\nhistory for the route migration finds a \"tracker:\" commit.\n\nContents are NOT mixed (ops in one commit, code in the other) and dev is\ncorrect: 72 passed / 11 xfailed, both CHANGELOG entries present, all four\nmigrations in place. This is a HISTORY-LEGIBILITY defect, not a correctness one.\n\nSECOND-ORDER FAILURE -- the git-notes recovery captured nothing useful.\nauto-pr's \"attach the original commit body\" step reads the body at merge time,\nby which point the amend had already replaced it, so the note reads:\n\n    Original commit body from f9e56d1509...:\n    Signed-off-by: jgstern-agent <josh-agent@iterabloom.com>\n\ni.e. the exact mechanism that exists to survive message loss recorded the\npost-loss state. The real message was recoverable only because it happened to\nstill exist in a scratch file; it has since been appended to the note by hand.\n\nAGENTS.md documents the OPPOSITE direction of this hazard (\"auto-pr rebase\ncopies the .ops dirs and restores them afterwards, silently overwriting any\ntracker mutation performed during the run\") and prescribes \"do not perform\ntracker mutations while an auto-pr run is in flight.\" That rule was FOLLOWED\nhere -- the `tracker add` for WI-basat completed before auto-pr started. The\nauto-sync fired on its own schedule (the 80-line pending-ops threshold) once\nauto-pr was already running. So the documented mitigation does not cover this\ncase, because the agent does not control when auto-sync fires.\n\nCandidate fixes, roughly in order of directness:\n  (a) auto-sync must never `--amend`. If HEAD is not a commit auto-sync itself\n      authored, it should create a NEW commit. An amend of someone else's commit\n      is never the intent.\n  (b) auto-sync should refuse to run while `.git/PR_PENDING` exists -- the gate\n      file auto-pr already maintains -- and defer until it clears. This is the\n      symmetric partner of the existing \"don't mutate the tracker during\n      auto-pr\" rule, enforced in code instead of by agent discipline.\n  (c) auto-pr should capture the commit body BEFORE it begins, not at merge\n      time, so the notes net cannot record a post-corruption state.\n(a) and (c) are independent and both worth doing; (c) makes the class of failure\nsurvivable even if some other mechanism rewrites a message.\n\nCannot be repaired in history: dev is protected and force-push is forbidden. The\nrationale now lives in the git note on cf955a0be1 and in CHANGELOG.md."  # 72be
    fields: {}  # 72be
- op: update  # f566
  at: '2026-07-31T00:26:35Z'  # f566
  by: agent  # f566
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f566
  clock: 2  # f566
  nonce: f566  # f566
  set:  # f566
    status: needs_human_review  # f566
    description: "CORRECTED 2026-07-30 after a premise-check. The original filing named the wrong\nmechanism and all three of its candidate fixes were wrong. The forensics below\nreplace it. (The original text remains in this item's append-only op log.)\n\nROOT CAUSE\n\n`scripts/auto-pr` amends HEAD unconditionally at three sites (auto-pr:1030,\n:1430, :1469 — all `git commit --amend --no-edit -s`). None checks that HEAD is\na commit the current branch actually owns. When a feature branch has no commits\nof its own, HEAD is still the base commit inherited from dev by `git checkout\n-b`, and the amend rewrites THAT commit: staged work is folded into it and it\nkeeps the base commit's message, author, and author-date.\n\nWhatever happened to be dev's tip gets impersonated. On 2026-07-29 dev's tip was\na tracker sync commit, so the code commit wore a \"tracker:\" subject — but\nnothing here is tracker-specific. The same hole would impersonate a feature,\ndocs, or release commit just as readily.\n\nEVIDENCE 1 — reflog (raw, .git/logs/HEAD lines 4829-4833)\n\n  a1d83f5e -> 4062aa43b8   merge origin/dev: Fast-forward             t=1785312991 (on dev)\n  4062aa43b8 -> 4062aa43b8 checkout: dev -> .../route-kind-slot-sweep-batch1  t=1785313007\n  4062aa43b8 -> f9e56d1509 commit (amend): tracker: 6 files (104 ops) t=1785314397\n  f9e56d1509 -> 4062aa43b8 checkout: .../batch1 -> dev                t=1785314649\n\nThe plain \"commit:\" entry is MISSING. Every other branch that day shows\ncheckout -> commit -> commit (amend) -> checkout (reflog lines 145-147, 140-142,\n134-136). This branch shows checkout -> commit (amend) -> checkout, with 23\nminutes of work in between and no commit of its own. f9e56d1509 is the local\nsha; the forge rebase produced cf955a0be1, which is why the git note reads\n\"Original commit body from f9e56d1509\".\n\nEVIDENCE 2 — commit objects\n\n  cf955a0be1  parent 4062aa43b8   author date 1785312952   committer Joshua G. Stern\n  4062aa43b8  parent a1d83f5e6d   author date 1785312952   committer Joshua G. Stern\n\ncf955a0be1 is a CHILD of 4062aa43b8, not a replacement of it — an amend of\n4062aa43b8 would have inherited a1d83f5e6d as its parent. The identical author\ndate is the amend's fingerprint: `--amend` preserves author identity and\nauthor-date while issuing a fresh committer-date.\n\nDISPOSITION OF THE THREE ORIGINALLY-FILED CANDIDATES\n\n(a) \"auto-sync must never --amend\" — NO-OP; there is nothing to fix. The tracker\n    contains zero `--amend` calls: grep over\n    packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/ and scripts/tracker both return empty.\n    do_sync has used plumbing (read-tree / write-tree / commit-tree against a\n    temporary index, no checkout) since e24407aef7 on 2026-03-06 — five months\n    before this incident. Its docstring states the intent outright: \"avoids\n    checkout, keeps working tree on the feature branch.\"\n\n(b) \"auto-sync should refuse to run while .git/PR_PENDING exists\" — ORTHOGONAL;\n    did not cause this. The sync's fast-forward landed at t=1785312991, sixteen\n    seconds BEFORE the branch was created and well before auto-pr ran. Nothing\n    was concurrent. (b) addresses a different hazard that AGENTS.md documents;\n    it is not this one.\n\n(c) \"auto-pr should capture the commit body BEFORE it begins\" — ALREADY THE\n    BEHAVIOR, and it did not help. DESC is assigned from `git log -1 --pretty=%b`\n    at auto-pr:1428, before the amend at :1430, and _attach_git_note\n    (forgejo-api.sh:1807) receives the body as a parameter. The note recorded a\n    lone sign-off trailer not because it read too late, but because there was\n    never a good message to read: HEAD was the inherited tracker commit from the\n    moment the branch was created.\n\nPROPOSED FIX (a-prime) — GOVERNANCE-GATED, AWAITING APPROVAL\n\nRefuse to amend a commit the branch does not own. Guard each of the three amend\nsites:\n\n    if git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD \"$base_ref\" 2>/dev/null; then\n        echo \"Refusing to amend: HEAD is contained in $base_ref;\"\n        echo \"this branch has no commits of its own. Commit first.\"\n        exit 1\n    fi\n\n`merge-base --is-ancestor` is the right predicate rather than a\n`rev-list --count` of base..HEAD: it is true exactly when HEAD is already\ncontained in the base branch, which is the failure condition, and it stays\ncorrect across rebases and the failover base-ref swap.\n\nStructural in the AGENTS.md sense: it closes the hole whether the amend was\nissued by auto-pr's manifest step or typed by hand.\n\nSCOPE NOTE: filed as [infra] with a tracker framing. The defect is in\nscripts/auto-pr and is not tracker-specific. The title's \"tracker auto-sync\namended...\" clause is wrong and should be re-titled on approval.\n\nCannot be repaired in history: dev is protected and force-push is forbidden. The\nrationale lives in the git note on cf955a0be1 and in CHANGELOG.md."  # f566
- op: discuss  # 56e1
  at: '2026-07-31T00:26:35Z'  # 56e1
  by: agent  # 56e1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 56e1
  clock: 3  # 56e1
  nonce: '56e1'  # 56e1
  message: "Premise-checked before implementing (L1). The filing's mechanism is wrong, and so are all three of its candidate fixes. Description replaced with the forensics; summary:\n\nROOT CAUSE. Not the tracker. `scripts/auto-pr` amends HEAD unconditionally at three sites (:1030, :1430, :1469) with no check that HEAD is a commit the branch owns. A branch created by `git checkout -b` from dev inherits dev's tip as HEAD; if no commit of its own has been made yet, the amend rewrites the INHERITED commit -- folding staged work into it while keeping its message, author and author-date. Dev's tip happened to be a tracker sync commit, which is the only reason this looked tracker-shaped. The same hole impersonates any dev tip.\n\nDECISIVE EVIDENCE. The reflog for that branch is checkout -> commit (amend) -> checkout. The plain `commit:` entry is absent, while every other branch that day shows checkout -> commit -> commit (amend) -> checkout. 23 minutes of work, no commit of its own. Corroborated by the objects: cf955a0be1's parent IS 4062aa43b8 (a child, not a replacement -- an amend of 4062 would have taken a1d83f5e as parent) and both carry author date 1785312952, which is the amend fingerprint.\n\nTHE THREE FILED FIXES.\n(a) \"auto-sync must never --amend\" -- no-op. The tracker has zero `--amend` calls anywhere; do_sync has been plumbing-based with no checkout since 2026-03-06 (e24407aef7), five months before the incident.\n(b) \"auto-sync should defer while PR_PENDING exists\" -- orthogonal. The sync's fast-forward preceded the branch creation by 16 seconds; nothing was concurrent. Still arguably worth doing on its own merits, but it would not have prevented this.\n(c) \"capture the body before auto-pr begins\" -- already the behavior. DESC is read at :1428, before the amend at :1430. The note captured a bare sign-off because there was never a good message to read, not because it read late.\n\nPROPOSED FIX, AND WHY I HAVE NOT WRITTEN IT. The fix is a guard before each amend site refusing to amend when `git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD \"$base_ref\"` is true. `scripts/auto-pr` is a governance file, so per the AGENTS.md approval workflow I have set this item to needs_human_review rather than opening a PR. Requesting explicit approval to proceed.\n\nTwo things worth your ruling beyond the code:\n1. The title still says \"tracker auto-sync amended a feature-branch commit\". That is false. Re-title on approval to something like \"auto-pr amends HEAD without checking the branch owns it; impersonates whatever dev's tip is\".\n2. Whether to also take (b). It is real per AGENTS.md's own documented hazard, just not this bug.\n\nNote I did not establish whether the amend was issued by auto-pr's manifest step or typed by hand -- the reflog cannot distinguish them. It does not change the fix: the guard closes the hole either way, which is the point of fixing it structurally."  # 56e1
