- op: discuss  # 1b9a
  at: '2026-07-31T00:27:34Z'  # 1b9a
  by: agent  # 1b9a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1b9a
  clock: 5  # 1b9a
  nonce: 1b9a  # 1b9a
  message: "Live repro + predicate validation, in a throwaway repo (no network, no forge):\n\n  git init -b dev; commit \"feat: a real base commit\"\n  git checkout -b feature          # no commit of its own\n  echo work > b.txt; git add b.txt\n  git commit --amend --no-edit\n  git log -1 --pretty=%s   ->   \"feat: a real base commit\"\n\nThe work lands wearing the BASE commit's subject. That is WI-libok's damage\nreproduced from scratch, with no tracker involved anywhere -- confirming the\ndefect is generic to auto-pr's amend, not tracker-shaped.\n\nGuard predicate validated on both arms:\n  branch with no commits of its own  -> merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD dev TRUE  (guard fires, correct)\n  branch with its own commit         -> merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD dev FALSE (guard silent, correct)\n\nSo the proposed guard catches the failure and does not block the normal flow.\n\nAlso re-titled this item -- the old title asserted the tracker did it, which the\nforensics disprove, and leaving a known-false title in place is the exact\ndeferral the decision register's calibration note warns about. Revert if you\ndisagree; the reasoning is in the description."  # 1b9a
